menu "Thread Manager"

    config THREAD_MANAGER_LEAF_DATA_POLL_PERIOD_MS
        int "LEAF Thread SED MAC data poll period (ms)"
        default 500
        help
            otLinkSetPollPeriod() value applied to every LEAF join
            (components/thread_manager's thread_manager_join_with_dataset(),
            when its own thread_data_poll_period_ms argument is 0) -- how
            often this SED wakes its radio to ask its parent whether it has
            anything queued for it.

            This is DELIBERATELY INDEPENDENT of any sensor measurement/
            sampling period (see child_service's own POLL_CONFIG handling
            and sensor_service) -- a real-hardware finding showed that
            reusing a multi-second sensor sampling period here made this
            device's own CoAP client (sensor_transport/topology_reporter)
            give up waiting for a response before this device's next data
            poll could even retrieve it from its parent, well before any
            data was actually lost. Keep this comfortably shorter than
            CONFIG_SENSOR_COAP_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS (components/
            coap_response_timing) -- see docs/power-base.md's SED CoAP
            response timing section. May be tuned lower for responsiveness
            or higher for power savings once real measurements are
            available; this Kconfig default (500ms) is a prototype value,
            not a measured optimum.

endmenu
